   "_dt": 1795139223.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "HD Hyundai Heavy Industries said Friday a U.S. maritime delegation visited its shipyard to discuss cooperation in shipbuilding, military logistics and port infrastructure. Johnson, deputy administrator of the U.S. Maritime Administration (MARAD), toured the shipyard in Ulsan, about 360 kilometers southeast of Seoul, on Thursday. Last month, HD Hyundai signed an agreement with U.S. engineering and construction firm Kiewit to establish a joint venture to build a shipyard in the United States.",
   "summary_zh": "HD Hyundai Heavy Industries周五表示，美国海事代表团到访其船厂，讨论在造船、军事后勤和港口基础设施方面的合作。美国海事管理局（MARAD）副局长Johnson于周四参观了位于首尔东南约360公里的蔚山船厂。上个月，HD Hyundai与美国工程建筑公司Kiewit签署协议，将成立一家合资企业，在美国建设船厂。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "HD Hyundai Heavy Industries said Friday a U.S. maritime delegation visited its shipyard to discuss cooperation in shipbuilding, military logistics and port infrastructure. The delegation, led by Mark D. Johnson, deputy administrator of the U.S. Maritime Administration (MARAD), toured the shipyard in Ulsan, about 360 kilometers southeast of Seoul, on Thursday. MARAD, an agency under the U.S. Department of Transportation, oversees maritime transport of military supplies during national emergencies and supports port infrastructure development. The visit came as Washington pushes to rebuild its domestic shipbuilding industry under its \"Bridge Strategy,\" which seeks to leverage the shipbuilding expertise and production capacity of allies while expanding its own industrial base. Last month, HD Hyundai signed an agreement with U.S. engineering and construction firm Kiewit to establish a joint venture to build a shipyard in the United States. Construction is scheduled to begin next year, with full-scale operations targeted for 2029",
