   "summary": "Unionized workers at Seoul Metro launched a \"work-to-rule\" campaign Friday as they remain locked in a dispute with management over hiring and wages. Under the collective action that began at 6 a.m., participants will fully adhere to safety regulations, such as maintaining train speeds regardless of subway schedules, in a move expected to slow down operations.",
   "summary_zh": "首尔地铁工会成员于星期五发起“按规章工作”行动，因为他们与管理层在招聘和工资问题上仍陷入僵局。这项集体行动于上午6时开始，参与者将严格遵守安全规定，例如无论地铁时刻表如何安排，都将保持列车运行速度；预计此举将减缓运营。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Unionized workers at Seoul Metro launched a \"work-to-rule\" campaign Friday as they remain locked in a dispute with management over hiring and wages. Under the collective action that began at 6 a.m., participants will fully adhere to safety regulations, such as maintaining train speeds regardless of subway schedules, in a move expected to slow down operations. The union plans to continue the collective action and launch an indefinite strike next Wednesday unless the management responds to its demands for an additional hiring of 1,313 personnel and a wage increase of 3.5 percent. It has also called for the management to scrap a plan to cut 2,212 jobs. Unionized workers of Korea Railroad Corp. (KORAIL) have also warned of launching an indefinite general strike on Dec. 10, demanding the hiring of more safety-related personnel",
