   "title": "Producer prices drop in Oct. on lower food prices",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/economy/20261120/producer-prices-drop-in-oct-on-lower-food-prices",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:47:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795139223.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "Producer prices fell for the first time in three months in October, driven by lower prices of agricultural goods on mild weather conditions, central bank data showed Friday. From a year earlier, producer prices rose 7.2 percent in October, slowing from the previous month's 7.6 percent on-year gain, the latest findings showed. Producer prices are a key indicator of future inflation trends, as they influence the prices businesses charge consumers in the months ahead.",
   "summary_zh": "中央银行周五公布的数据显示，受温和天气条件下农产品价格下跌的推动，10月生产者价格三年来首次下降。最新调查结果显示，10月生产者价格较上年同期上涨7.2%，低于上月7.6%的同比涨幅。生产者价格是未来通胀趋势的一项关键指标，因为它们会影响企业未来数月向消费者收取的价格。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Producer prices fell for the first time in three months in October, driven by lower prices of agricultural goods on mild weather conditions, central bank data showed Friday. The producer price index (PPI), a key gauge of future consumer inflation, dropped 0.1 percent last month from a month earlier, following a 0.1 percent on-month gain each in August and September, according to the preliminary data from the Bank of Korea (BOK). The index had risen for 10 consecutive months since September 2025 and fell in July. From a year earlier, producer prices rose 7.2 percent in October, slowing from the previous month's 7.6 percent on-year gain, the latest findings showed. Producer prices are a key indicator of future inflation trends, as they influence the prices businesses charge consumers in the months ahead. The BOK said prices of agricultural, livestock and fisheries products declined 8.3 percent in October due to increased supply of fruit amid good weather and decreased demand for pork after the Chuseok holiday in September. Prices of electricity, gas and water supplies climbed 0.2 percent last month. Prices of industrial goods, including petroleum and chemical products, gained 0.3 percent in October from a month earlier. The domestic supply price index, which reflects both producer and import prices, added 0.7 percent in October from a month earlier, the data showed",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "eco",
    "ene"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
