   "summary": "The domestic stock market extended its negative performance yesterday , as sustained selling pressure dragged the major market indicator lower by 0.02 per cent. Consequently, market capitalisation decreased by N28 billion to close at N161.21 trillion. Market sentiment remained negative, with 26 decliners, outnumbering 19 advancers.",
   "summary_zh": "国内股市昨日延续跌势，持续的抛售压力拖累主要市场指标下跌0.02%。因此，市值减少280亿奈拉，收于161.21万亿奈拉。市场情绪仍然低迷，26只股票下跌，数量超过19只上涨的股票。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The domestic stock market extended its negative performance yesterday , as sustained selling pressure dragged the major market indicator lower by 0.02 per cent. The Nigerian Exchange Limited All-Share Index (NGX ASI) declined by 43.09 basis points, or 0.02 per cent to close at 248,286.56 basis points. Consequently, market capitalisation decreased by N28 billion to close at N161.21 trillion. Sectoral performance was mixed, as the Insurance (+1.7per cent) and Industrial Goods (+0.1per cent) indices advanced, while the Consumer Goods (-0.3per cent) and Oil & Gas (-0.1per cent) indices declined. Meanwhile the Banking index closed flat. Market sentiment remained negative, with 26 decliners, outnumbering 19 advancers. Sovereign Trust Insurance led the gainers’ chart, rising 9.96 per cent to close at N2.76, per share. Critical Minerals Financing Corporation (CMFC) followed with a gain of 9.94 per cent to close at N3.87, while Chellarams rose 9.86 per cent to close at N11.70, per share. Cornerstone Insurance advanced by 9.64 per cent to close at N4.55, while Regency Alliance Insurance gained 8.45 per cent to close at 77 kobo, per share. On the losers’ side, Royal Exchange led the decline, falling by 6.00 per cent to close at 94 kobo, per share. McNichols followed with a decline of 5.05 per cent to close at N4.70, while International Breweries depreciated by 4.50 per cent to close at N9.55, per share. Veritas Kapital Assurance shed 4.42 per cent to close at N1.08, while Oando lost 4.17 per cent to close at N34.50, per share. Also, the total volume of trade declined by 17.54 per cent to 372.030 million units, valued at N14.367 billion, and exchanged in 28,467 deals. Transactions in the shares of Trans-Nationwide Express led the activity with 30.251 million shares worth N74.121 million. Chams Holdings Company followed with account of 29.989 million shares valued at N90.908 million, while Fidelity Bank traded 20.097 million shares valued at N460.634 million. Guaranty Trust Holding Company (GTCO) traded 18.037 million shares worth N2.093 billion, while Sovereign Trust Insurance traded 17.715 million shares worth N47.692 million. Looking ahead, Cowry Assets Management Limited said, “weak market breadth, subdued trading activity, and lingering sell-side pressure may constrain near-term recovery, although selective bargain-hunting in fundamentally sound counters could provide some support. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
